    "Solid tumor, diabetes, kidney disease, cirrhosis, malnutrition, or nephrotic syndrome alone are context and cannot change an opportunistic candidate route.",
    "Opportunistic Audit-to-Context and Context-to-Priority require both rank at most ten and at least two positive tests with analytical reproducibility.",
    "HAP, HCAP, or airway-device history is setting context and never identifies a pathogen by itself.",
    "A setting-only hospital Gram-negative Context-to-Priority adjustment requires rank at most five plus at least two reproducible positive tests.",
    "A prior MDR record may use the rank-at-most-ten route only when its organism genus matches the candidate.",
    "Single-test hospital Gram-negative signals are not promoted by HAP or MDR history.",
    "At most two representatives per patient in each history family may be adjusted.",
    "History never creates a candidate and never directly creates Picked.",
    "Evidence consumed by this stage is recorded and cannot be counted again as an independent High-to-Picked axis.",
